z3660rtg: the Z3660's RTG as its own driver, /dev/z3660rtg, major 55

The Z3660 RTG and the MNT ZZ9000 become separate drivers, so a machine with
both boards has both (people may have more than one graphics card):

- the Z3660 rows only (AutoConfig 0x144B0001 and the fixed window on AGA);
  ZZ9K_TARGET_Z3660 is implied, the ZZ9000 rows and tables are gone;
- every global has its own name: z3660rtginit/open/close/read/write/ioctl/
  mmap, z3660rtgconsoleputc/consolewrite, z3660rtgvtinfo/vtpan/vtdirty,
  z3660rtg_blit_on/_blit_maxarea; the console lines say "z3660rtg:";
- the fixed window is probed with one caught bprobe() read first and is
  silent without a board (an A4000 without a Z3660 has empty Zorro III
  space there); -DZZ9K_DEBUG prints the old line.

The ioctl ABI (zz9000.h) is unchanged; the device node and major are the
kit's (cdevsw[55], port/src/patch_z3660rtg_cdevsw.py).

